al to be involved directly or  indirectly in the protests  through our partners across the country  were able to identify one individual and  interdict him before he was able to get  close to the city a firearm was seized  charges were laid and he will face full  prosecution including potential jail  time that remains for anybody in this  city or in this country or in any other  country that intends to bring a firearm  to a lawful protest  to engage in unlawful activity in any  way  do not bring weapons do not bring  firearms do not come here to cause harm  do not come here to break the law you  will be held to account  okay we have time for two more questions  uh hi craig lord from global news can  you clarify then do you currently have  intelligence that there are restricted  firearms planned to be in the city this  weekend when the protesters come i'm  going to invite deputy chiefs bell to  provide that intelligence update for you  uh thank you very much for the question  uh in terms of intelligence that we have  for this weekend we are receiving  information have been tracking and  working with our partners we're  anticipating between three to four  hundred trucks attempting to enter to  engage in in the demonstration this  weekend  we also have information that indicates  that there will be between one and two  thousand foot participants who will join  the the area of the demonstration as  well as up to a thousand counter  protesters who have indicated a desire  to come down to the area in terms of  specific intelligence that we have  relating to weapons and firearms we  continue to update the city in terms of  public safety advisories and conduct  investigations in any sort of weapons or  threat related uh information that we  receive thanks for the question  and the last question  hi chief it's joanne canelo from cbc  news um  chief uh i'm sure a lot of people are  very happy to hear there are efforts  being made to stop trucks coming into  the corps people h