ress  in reducing this number through  enforcement and patient negotiations  during the past week  we know more demonstrators plan to come  and want to be very clear that they  should stay home  based on our experience over the last  week we are implementing a range of  tactical measures to keep ottawa  residents safe  and prevent further unlawful activity  we are deploying all available police  resources  residents and demonstrators will see a  surge in on-duty officers in the  downtown neighborhoods of centertown  lower town and the byward market  on the ground this will represent an  officer on every street corner to fully  enforce all unlawful acts  officers have received zero tolerance  enforcement directives with full  authority to pursue the strictest  possible  punishments  for traffic violations  mischief  hate crimes  harassment  spitting intimidation and or menacing  behavior  to address incoming traffic we are  utilizing hundreds of concrete and heavy  equipment barricades to create  non-access roadways throughout  centertown and the byward market  the city of ottawa will further share  information on this initiative later  today  we are working to ensure the flow of  traffic but it may be necessary at times  to close the inter-provincial bridges  our negotiators have also communicated  designated parking zones to  demonstration organizers  the efforts of the ottawa police service  this weekend will be focused on the  unlawful behavior connected to the  demonstrations  and the possible influx of demonstrators  the ongoing occupation of the  parliamentary precinct  remains unsolved  unresolved and we are working with all  policing partners including the rcmp the  opp  to re to remove these vehicles as safely  and as quickly as possible  our top priority is to bring these  demonstrations to an end  i'll now turn it over to deputy chief  steve bell who will speak more about  what to anticipate this weekend as well  as our investigative actions given that  y