o we can make changes in real time i've  announced today real time massive  changes  150 officers surging into the three  impacted neighborhoods of centertown  lower town and the market on a 24 7  patrol focused on unlawful unacceptable  violent behavior affecting those  neighborhoods we have significantly  increased resources from provincial and  federal sources as well as our municipal  partners and we have new engaged allies  at all three levels of government and  across civil society it is that combined  effort that will continue the success to  date that we've had i will tell you the  first question a member of the media  asked me 12 days ago when it was clear  that this would be a sizable  demonstration coming to the nation's  capital  the very first question asked me by a  member of the media chief how will you  stop what happened on january 6 in  washington dc in 2020  and i got to tell you  that was stopped  now we've got a lot of unacceptable and  unlawful activities in addition to the  death injury and full riots that we saw  south of the border a year ago in almost  the same circumstances  i take no solace in that success i learn  from that and i learn from the mistakes  made  i gather more information i gather more  resources i gather more allies and every  day we wake up and try to do it better  we need to do it better and we will do  it better thank you very much for your  question  i think that's the two questions thank  you very much for watching  right there  yeah i'll get it  okay  that's all the time we have situated  we will be taking one-on-ones with  deputy bell and deputy ferguson  ferguson  ferguson the english ones will  facilitate with  deputy chief bill thank you  okay
 

